// SR 281.1 — Title Ten Avoidance
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:PATH
A. Principles
|

:NOTE
Amended by No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455).
|

:INFO
Art. 285
1 Avoidance actions aim to make assets subject to enforcement proceedings where they have been made unavailable by means of a legal act under Articles 286–288.
2 The following persons are entitled to bring an avoidance action:
1. any creditor who has received a provisional or definitive unpaid debt certificate in distraint proceedings;
2. the bankruptcy administration or, in accordance with the Articles 260 and 269 paragraph 3, any individual creditor in bankruptcy.
3 Avoidance actions may not be brought in the case of legal acts that were carried out during a composition moratorium if they were approved by a composition court or by a creditors’ committee (Art. 295a).
4 Other liabilities entered into during the moratorium with the consent of the commissioner are also not subject to avoidance.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 2 let. 1 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 3 — Term pursuant to No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455). This amendment has been made throughout the text.
Para. 3 — Inserted by No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455).
Para. 4 — Inserted by Annex No 4 of the FA of 19 June 2020 (Company Law), in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2020 4005; 2022 109; BBl 2017 399).

:PATH
B. Types

:PATH
1. Avoidance of a gift
|

:INFO
Art. 286
1 With the exception of customary occasional gifts, all gifts and gratuitous dispositions made by the debtor within the last year prior to distraint or the declaration of bankruptcy are subject to avoidance.
2 The following are treated in the same way as gifts:
1. legal transactions by which the debtor has accepted a consideration that is disproportionate to his own performance;
2. legal transactions through which the debtor has acquired a life annuity, lifetime maintenance, a usufruct or a right of residence for himself or for a third party.
3 If an action in favour of a close associate or relative of the debtor is contested, the latter bears the burden of proof that there is no imbalance between performance and consideration. Close associates also include companies within a group.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 2 let. 2 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 3 — Inserted by No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455).

:PATH
2. Avoidance for overindebtedness
|

:INFO
Art. 287
1 The following legal acts are subject to avoidance if the debtor performed them within the last year before distraint or the declaration of bankruptcy and was already overindebted at the time they were performed:
1. provision of security for existing liabilities that the debtor was not previously obliged to provide;
2. repayment of a monetary debt by means other than cash or other customary means of payment;
3. payment of a debt that is not yet due.
2 However, avoidance is excluded if the beneficiary proves that he did not know and should not have known of the debtor’s overindebtedness.
|

:INFO
Art. 287 (continued)
3 Avoidance is excluded in particular if securities, intermediated securities or other financial instruments traded on a representative market have been provided as collateral and the debtor has previously:
1. undertaken to increase the collateral in the event of changes in the value of the collateral or in the amount of the secured liability; or
2. been granted the right to replace collateral with collateral of the same value.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 1 let. 1 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 3 let. 2 — Inserted by Annex No 4 of the Intermediated Securities Act of 3 Oct. 2008, in force since 1 Jan. 2010 (AS 2009 3577; BBl 2006 9315).

:PATH
3. Avoidance of wilful unlawful acts
|

:INFO
Art. 288
1 Any legal acts that the debtor carried out within the five years before distraint or the declaration of bankruptcy with the intention, recognisable to the other party, of prejudicing his creditors or favouring individual creditors to the prejudice of the others are ultimately subject to avoidance.
2 When seeking avoidance of an act in favour of a close associate or relative of the debtor, the associate or relative bears the burden of proving that the intention to cause prejudice was not recognisable. Close associates also include companies in a group of companies.
|

:NOTE
Art. 288 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).
Para. 2 — Inserted by No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455).

:PATH
4. Calculation of the relevant periods
|

:INFO
Art. 288a
The following are not considered when calculating the relevant periods under Articles 286–288:
1. the duration of any preceding composition moratorium;
2. in the case of liquidation of an estate by the bankruptcy office, the time between the date of death and ordering liquidation;
3. the duration of the prior debt enforcement proceedings.
|

:NOTE
Art. 288a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1). Amended by No I of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2014 (AS 2013 4111; BBl 2010 6455).

:PATH
C. Avoidance action

:PATH
1. Place of jurisdiction
|

:INFO
Art. 289
The avoidance action shall be filed in the court at the domicile of the defendant. If the defendant is not domiciled in Switzerland, the action may be filed in the court at the place of the distraint or bankruptcy proceedings.
|

:NOTE
Art. 289 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).

:PATH
2. Respondents
|

:INFO
Art. 290
An avoidance action may be brought against persons who have concluded legal transactions subject to avoidance with the debtor or who have been favoured by the debtor in a manner subject to avoidance, as well as against their heirs or other general successors and against third parties acting in bad faith. The rights of third parties acting in good faith are not affected by an avoidance action.
|

:NOTE
Art. 290 — Amended by No I of the FA of 16 Dec. 1994, in force since 1 Jan. 1997 (AS 1995 1227; BBl 1991 III 1).

:PATH
D. Effect
|

:INFO
Art. 291
1 Any person who has acquired any of the debtor’s assets through a legal act subject to avoidance is obliged to return them. The consideration must be reimbursed to the extent that it is still in the hands of the debtor or the debtor has been enriched by it. Otherwise, reimbursement may only be claimed as a debt due by the debtor.
2 If the legal act subject to avoidance consisted in the repayment of a debt, the debt shall be reinstated upon restitution of the amount received.
3 The bona fide recipient of a gift is only obliged to make restitution up to the amount of his enrichment.

:PATH
E. Statute of limitations
|

:INFO
Art. 292
1 The right to seek avoidance becomes time-barred:
1. on expiry of three years from service of the unpaid debt certificate in distraint proceedings (Art. 285 para. 2 no 1);
2. on expiry of three years from the declaration of bankruptcy (Art. 285 para. 2 no 2);
3. on expiry of three years from confirmation of the composition agreement with assignment of assets.
2 When recognising a foreign bankruptcy decree, the time between the application for recognition and publication in accordance with Article 169 PILA is not taken into account.
|

:NOTE
Art. 292 — Amended by No III of the FA of 15 June 2018 (Revision of the Statute of Limitations), in force since 1 Jan. 2020 (AS 2018 5343; BBl 2014 235).
Para. 2 — SR 291

